      "writtenOn": "2016-12-14T02:05:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Something seems amiss here.\n\n- Given the comment at line 345, I\u0027d expect this function to be called |enableRoamingControl|, rather than |enableRoaming|.\n\n- But, examining wifi_hal.h in hardware_legacy, I don\u0027t see a function with either name. Instead, I see |wifi_enable_firmware_roaming|.\n\n- My expectations for functions with these names are quite different. enableRoamingControl() seems like it would toggle between default firmware behavior, and customized firmware behavior (per StaRomaingConfig). enableFirmwareRoaming() seems like it would toggle firmware roaming on or off entirely.\n\nSo I\u0027m not really sure what to expect of this function.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 356,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 356,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "9419a623e196c76d88e3c50405d9e9391dfefda3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba845725_0485ea98",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/IWifiStaIface.hal",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 356,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-12-14T02:32:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "enableRoamingControl seems to be the best name for this method\u0027s functionality because we\u0027re giving control over all roaming decisions to firmware. I didn\u0027t want to use the term firmware here (even though it\u0027s used in the legacy HAL) because this doesn\u0027t necessarily have to be tied to firmware. This can also be done by the driver for example.",
      "parentUuid": "ba845725_f9116373",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 356,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 356,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "9419a623e196c76d88e3c50405d9e9391dfefda3",
